add('1734-Q03','sourceSupport','The literal (1.5,1.5) mm target has radius 0.002121 m and is reachable for 1 m links, while the keyed option incorrectly asserts 2.12 m. Mark the radial-workspace derivation as a premise/derived use of FK, not an explicit printed workspace formula, and cite the actual metre-link source.')
add('1735-Q02','sourceSupport figureFidelity','The actual panel is explicitly x(m),y(m) with 1 m links. Rounded angles give approximately(0.4143,1.3509) m, so the genuine small difference is only rounding. Add page 1734 for the FK equation retained in the solution; do not reinterpret the current thousandfold unit mismatch as harmless rounding.')
add('1739-Q03','assumptions','Clarify physical error versus blindly executing a unit-inappropriate print expression: the literal residuals have mean0.025 mm=0.0025 cm. Passing their raw numbers to the unmodified metre-assuming *100 expression would print2.50 cm but that would be a mislabeled result, not their physical mean. The current solution instead silently changes the inputs to metres. Correct the question or explicitly test that dimensional bug; do not claim all literal code-output interpretations are impossible.')
add('1740-Q02','sourceSupport','The offered (pi/2,pi/2) pair reaches(-1,1) m with the source links, not millimetres. Add an exact1 m link premise from page1731/1735 or explicitly supply it in the corrected question.')
add('1740-Q04','sourceSupport','Literal mm-coordinate differences give approximately0.015744 cm, whereas the source metre endpoint error is15.74447 cm. Add page1734 for FK and page1739 for Euclidean evaluation if retaining those formulas. Narrow the solution metadata to this single-sample error rather than importing an unrelated sample-mean formula; the given endpoint already reduces the current calculation to a direct norm/conversion.')
add('1720-Q02','distractors','Make the alternatives parallel sensor-to-task mappings. The only three-part application answer competes with a lone torque-as-position claim and encoder-as-force/load-cell-as-angle claims; these are visibly different task/quantity errors rather than credible competing application mappings. Preserve the correct source-specific, nonexclusive mapping.')
add('1721-Q01','distractors','Replace the vacuum-welding-current/welding-suction-pressure swap with plausible same-tool alternatives, such as pressure versus flow/seal inference and electrical/process channels versus pose-only sensing. Avoid making a cross-domain tool-name swap the main distractor.')
